 "text": "Brief reasoning for each question:\n\n1. Angular velocity ω = 2π × 10 / 60 ≈ 1.047 rad s⁻¹. **A**\n2. \"তাপসী\" is a play by দ্বিজেন্দ্রলাল রায়. **B**\n3. Chlorine has atomic number 17, so it has 17 protons and 35 − 17 = 18 neutrons. **A**\n4. The net displacement is 20 miles north and 12 miles east. That gives √544 ≈ 23.3 miles, which matches none of the options. I chose ২০ as the closest intended answer, but this is a guess. **D**\n5. Loading fork A reduces the beats, so A has the higher frequency: 512 + 5 = 517 Hz. **D**\n6. \"Takes after\" means resembles. **C**\n7. a³ + 1/a³ = 4³ − 3·4 = 52. **B**\n8. Ornithology is the study of birds. **C**\n9. This is the Williamson ether synthesis. **B**\n10. d/dx[ln(sec x)] = sec x tan x / sec x = tan x. **D**\n11. The Earth's magnetic south pole lies near Hudson Bay in northern Canada. **B**\n12. বঙ্গভাষা is a sonnet written in অক্ষরবৃত্ত, not মাত্রাবৃত্ত. **A**\n13. Calcutta's first theatre (the Playhouse) was built in 1753. **D**\n14. আ হ ম মোস্তফা কামাল was the first Bangladeshi ICC president. **B**\n15. Taking the start as facing north: 10 ft east, 20 ft north, 20 ft west, 20 ft south. He ends 10 ft west of A. **C**\n\n{\"answers\": {\"33ee0f6d-2208-4252-a253-52aa63720948-3812\": \"A\", \"349d2a82-086f-4bdd-a8c9-e3a807fd6c42-87597\": \"B\", \"37f12437-63ed-47d2-822d-e43efb5fc695-124481\": \"A\", \"3b374461-0318-4d76-8666-87185e36ae19-7268\": \"D\", \"3baddf77-158e-4c58-835d-bcf0966f61e2-46524\": \"D\", \"3c022c34-fa81-495b-a405-f8f6b74b8440-38265\": \"C\", \"3c23fdab-d090-40b9-aa1c-b170c1aeb27b-124238\": \"B\", \"3cc94f03-794f-49ce-8f5c-7b54051d99b3-8217\": \"C\", \"3d7e7041-55fa-4705-a956-07dbc67e3322-8053\": \"B\", \"3d802074-f841-4127-8ab8-dc73f830b286-38317\": \"D\", \"403644e4-0efa-4dd2-b773-e183a64969dc-68991\": \"B\", \"40865a63-8ab2-4409-bd3d-80b3cf488669-114511\": \"A\", \"40946678-c005-4e30-9b51-0cd751ab48dd-12237\": \"D\", \"40aa3b5f-e298-46d5-8e84-fc43b885dcab-61418\": \"B\", \"4101a41c-2881-4ead